---
output: svg
---
@startuml
' The package "outer" only holds "inner", so it is packed and drawn as the
' single package "outer.inner". Removing "Gone" leaves "outer.inner" empty,
' so it becomes a plain node. Graphviz writes the content of a packed package
' at its own position among the sibling packages, after "sib". Smetana must do
' the same, so "sib" stays on the left as with Graphviz: in the reference SVG
' the title "sib" has a smaller x than "outer.inner".
!pragma layout smetana
!pragma useIntermediatePackages false
package sib {
  class S
}
package outer {
  package inner {
    class Gone $gone
  }
}
remove $gone
@enduml
